<title>ARGENTINA: U.S. Exxel Group buys Argentine health care firm.</title>
<headline>U.S. Exxel Group buys Argentine health care firm.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. investment group Exxel said it bought on Tuesday the Argentine health care firm TIM for $40 million.</p>
<p>With this operation The Exxel Group adds TIM's 85,000 clients making a total of 170,000 in Argentina, an Exxel spokeswoman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The deal will increase Exxel's annual revenues in Argentina to $246.</p>
<p>Exxel, which had no stake in TIM, bought all the shares of the health care firm.</p>
<p>The group is the largest in the Argentine health care sector. It also owns several clinics and health care firms.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Hskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
